**Best Practices for Exception Handling**:
```java
// ✓ Good: Specific exception handling
try {
    int value = Integer.parseInt(input);
} catch (NumberFormatException e) {
    System.out.println("Invalid number format");
}

// ✗ Avoid: Empty catch block
try {
    riskyOperation();
} catch (Exception e) {
    // Silent failure - bad practice
}

// ✓ Good: Log exception and provide context
try {
    operation();
} catch (Exception e) {
    logger.error("Operation failed for user: " + userId, e);
    throw new BusinessException("Operation failed", e);
}

// ✓ Good: Throw checked exception as unchecked
try {
    Thread.sleep(1000);
} catch (InterruptedException e) {
    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
    throw new RuntimeException("Thread interrupted", e);
}

// ✗ Avoid: Catching too broad exceptions
