    // Multiple lines of code
} catch (Exception e) {  // Too broad!
}

// ✓ Good: Resource management
try (AutoCloseable resource = getResource()) {
    // Use resource
} catch (Exception e) {
    // Handle error
}
// resource.close() called automatically
```

**Key Points**:
- Handle exceptions close to where they occur
- Avoid empty catch blocks
- Log exceptions with context
- Clean up resources in finally or try-with-resources
- Throw checked exceptions, catch unchecked if appropriate
- Provide meaningful error messages to users
